## Elasticsearch index mapping recommendation

Spring Data will create a usable mapping, but for production I recommend explicitly creating it:

```json
PUT connection-registry
{
    "mappings": {
        "properties": {
            "name": { "type": "keyword" },
            "sourceType": { "type": "keyword" },
            "category": { "type": "keyword" },
            "host": { "type": "keyword" },
            "port": { "type": "integer" },
            "databaseName": { "type": "keyword" },
            "username": { "type": "keyword" },
            "encryptedSecret": { "type": "binary" },
            "sslEnabled": { "type": "boolean" },
            "properties": { "type": "object", "enabled": true },
            "createdAt": { "type": "date" },
            "updatedAt": { "type": "date" },
            "createdBy": { "type": "keyword" },
            "lastConnectionStatus": { "type": "keyword" },
            "lastConnectionMessage": { "type": "text", "index": false }
        }
    }
}
